      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The level of amputation is important in walking. Neurologic and cardiovascular deficits may limit the potential for ambulation. The remaining foot and joints must be protected. A variety of skin problems occur; diligent stump care prevents most of them. Phantom sensation is a normal phenomenon and usually resolves. Patients with pain in the extremity before amputation are predisposed to phantom pain."},
